  "_comment": "The model catalog shipped with each Spark Swapper release. Every entry names the platforms it runs on, how to install it, how to start/stop it and the speeds its recipe publishes. {{USER}} and {{HOME}} are filled in from the site config (/etc/spark-swapper/models.json, openclaw.user / openclaw.home). A model with the same key in the site config is merged over the catalog entry field by field (the site wins); list a key in the site config's \"hidden_models\" to hide it. Speeds are tokens per second: decode = one request on its own, decode_concurrent = the total across `concurrency` requests.",

